WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
Marcus wants money for a family expense while keeping his life

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:09.080
policy. If his contract has sufficient available loan value and

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.560
he has the required rights, he can request a policy loan.

4
00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.560
The insurer advances money with the policy as security.

5
00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:21.160
This is different from an unrelated bank loan and different from

6
00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.360
withdrawing part of the policy's value.

7
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:28.740
Policy debt carries interest and affects

8
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:32.720
the amount ultimately available on surrender or death.

9
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.820
The face amount alone does not establish how much Marcus can

10
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:42.240
borrow. Read the current loan value, existing debt,

11
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.820
applicable rate and conditions before explaining the available amount.

12
00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:52.466
Assume a covered death benefit of two hundred thousand dollars.

13
00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:57.366
The policy has twenty thousand dollars of unpaid loan principal and

14
00:00:57.366 --> 00:01:00.266
one thousand dollars of accrued unpaid loan interest.

15
00:01:01.066 --> 00:01:05.018
With no other adjustments, the net benefit is one hundred seventy-nine

16
00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:09.686
thousand dollars. Leaving out the interest would overstate the payment.

17
00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:14.526
A policy loan does not always require scheduled repayment like a

18
00:01:14.526 --> 00:01:18.766
bank installment loan, but unpaid debt still has consequences.

19
00:01:19.926 --> 00:01:22.446
Interest can be added to principal under the contract.

20
00:01:23.526 --> 00:01:27.326
If debt consumes the available value, the policy can face termination

21
00:01:27.326 --> 00:01:30.646
under the applicable conditions and notice requirements.

22
00:01:32.146 --> 00:01:33.146
Monitor the actual statements.

23
00:01:33.972 --> 00:01:37.672
Marcus misses a premium after previously electing his policy's automatic

24
00:01:37.672 --> 00:01:42.652
premium loan provision. If the provision's conditions are met and enough

25
00:01:42.652 --> 00:01:46.572
value is available, the insurer makes a loan to pay that

26
00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:51.812
premium. The protection can continue, but the owner now

27
00:01:51.812 --> 00:01:54.312
owes policy debt and interest.

28
00:01:55.412 --> 00:01:57.812
This is not a free premium waiver.

29
00:01:59.112 --> 00:02:03.092
Maryland requires policies subject to its loan section to provide this

30
00:02:03.092 --> 00:02:08.312
provision, except the stated weekly-premium category, and makes its use

31
00:02:08.312 --> 00:02:11.252
subject to the entitled person's election.

32
00:02:12.092 --> 00:02:17.032
The section excludes term policies, term riders and industrial life.

33
00:02:17.972 --> 00:02:21.372
Do not present it as an automatic benefit on every life

34
00:02:21.372 --> 00:02:26.618
policy. Elena requests a partial withdrawal from a universal life policy

35
00:02:26.618 --> 00:02:30.618
that permits it. A withdrawal takes value out permanently under that

36
00:02:30.618 --> 00:02:33.558
transaction instead of recording a loan balance to repay.

37
00:02:34.458 --> 00:02:38.618
It may reduce the death benefit, incur charges and make future

38
00:02:38.618 --> 00:02:40.778
funding less secure under the contract.

39
00:02:41.738 --> 00:02:45.638
A full surrender instead ends the surrendered policy's protection.

40
00:02:46.518 --> 00:02:50.878
Whole life may allow access through different features, such as surrendering

41
00:02:50.878 --> 00:02:55.498
paid-up additions, rather than the same universal-life withdrawal mechanism.

42
00:02:55.978 --> 00:02:58.998
Identify the actual feature before quoting an effect.

43
00:02:59.958 --> 00:03:03.938
The same five thousand dollar cash need can produce different continuing

44
00:03:03.938 --> 00:03:06.438
obligations under a loan and a withdrawal.

45
00:03:07.536 --> 00:03:11.796
Marcus considers borrowing five thousand dollars against available policy

46
00:03:11.796 --> 00:03:13.616
value to help pay tuition.

47
00:03:14.596 --> 00:03:17.496
Paying a college bill does not transform that advance into a

48
00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:22.116
scholarship, federal student loan or tax-favored education account.

49
00:03:22.976 --> 00:03:26.636
It remains a policy loan with its own interest, effect on

50
00:03:26.636 --> 00:03:29.316
benefits and risk if debt grows.

51
00:03:30.316 --> 00:03:34.296
Compare the family's remaining protection needs and other funding resources

52
00:03:34.296 --> 00:03:39.376
before committing. The word educational describes the intended use

53
00:03:39.376 --> 00:03:43.716
in this example, not a universal separate policy rider.

54
00:03:44.716 --> 00:03:48.696
A producer should explain the real terms and avoid promising unlimited

55
00:03:48.696 --> 00:03:52.436
or cost-free access to the policy's death benefit.

56
00:03:53.126 --> 00:03:57.826
Maryland's modern policy-loan interest provision permits either the specified

57
00:03:57.826 --> 00:04:02.726
fixed maximum or an adjustable maximum calculated under the statute.

58
00:04:03.186 --> 00:04:07.166
Do not call six percent the universal cap for every policy

59
00:04:07.166 --> 00:04:11.846
loan. The contract must identify its applicable rate mechanism.

60
00:04:12.866 --> 00:04:16.006
Adjustable-rate loans have notice and adjustment rules.

61
00:04:16.786 --> 00:04:20.606
The standard loan provision also addresses termination when total debt

62
00:04:20.606 --> 00:04:24.506
reaches the loan value, including at least thirty days' notice to

63
00:04:24.506 --> 00:04:28.906
the specified parties. A loan for paying a premium is treated

64
00:04:28.906 --> 00:04:33.006
differently from other loans under the six-month deferral provision.

65
00:04:34.476 --> 00:04:38.826
Identify the transaction and controlling section before choosing a deadline

66
00:04:38.826 --> 00:04:40.646
or interest rule.
